<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<dependencies>
    <!--
        Daro Unity SDK — MAX mediation variant (Reward).

        Top-level artifacts only. Sub-network adapters and runtime support
        libraries are pinned transitively by each artifact's metadata.
        1:1 lock rule: one Daro version pins the full sub-network set.

        iOS: DaroObjCBridge — 통합 SDK 의 ObjC 표면 래퍼 xcframework.
             CocoaPods trunk 정식 좌표 2.0.0-rc.5 (임시 `:http =>` /
             `:podspec =>` 배선 없음). Unity shim 이 ObjC++ 라 Swift-only 인
             DaroAds 가 아니라 이 브리지를 문다 — DaroAds 를 같이 선언하면
             중복 설치된다.

             podspec 이 27개를 전이로 물고 온다: Google-Mobile-Ads-SDK +
             AppLovinSDK + 13개 네트워크의 AdMob·MAX 짝 어댑터(Facebook/
             ByteDance/InMobi/Fyber/IronSource/Vungle/Mintegral/Moloco/Line/
             UnityAds/PubMatic + Verve(MAX 단독)). 1:1 lock 규칙대로 여기서는
             최상위 하나만 선언한다.

             static_framework: true, 최소 iOS 13.0. `preserve_paths 'Scripts/*'`
             로 정본 훅 daro_integration_key.rb 와 daro CLI 가 실려 온다. order 45 가
             Podfile 에 post_install 을 걸고 pod install(order 50) 이 주입한다.

             레거시 DaroMObjCBridge 1.1.64 는 이전 세대다 — dynamic framework
             에 AmazonPublisherServicesSDK 를 물었고, 통합 세트는 APS 를
             제외한다(DARO-879).

        Android: so.daro:daro-sdk on Maven Central — unified SDK 2.0.
                 AdMob + MAX mediation coexist in the single artifact (no
                 build-time variant; per-request routing is a runtime server
                 policy), and daro-core sources are inlined into the
                 artifact, so nothing else needs declaring. The legacy
                 per-mediation artifact (so.daro:daro-m 1.3.x) is the
                 previous generation — replaced by DARO-1432.

                 Sub-network maven repos (8) are declared inside the
                 androidPackage's <repositories> block so EDM4U owns the
                 merge: Mode 1 (Unity ≤ 2022.x + Custom Template ON) injects
                 into mainTemplate.gradle / settingsTemplate.gradle; Mode 2
                 (Unity 2023.1+ no template) uses them at resolve time and
                 downloads AARs into Assets/Plugins/Android/Repos/. Either
                 way the SDK author's job ends with this declaration —
                 post-process patching the exported settings.gradle would
                 duplicate EDM4U's merge layer. The repo list mirrors the
                 unified adapter set (react-native/plugin/src/withAndroid.ts
                 and android/daro-android-qa/settings.gradle.kts): smaato /
                 chartboost dropped, verve / premiumads / pubmatic added
                 vs. the daro-m generation.

                 Out-of-scope for EDM4U (handled by DaroAndroidPostProcessor):
                 root buildscript.classpath (so.daro:daro-plugin +
                 AppLovinQualityServiceGradlePlugin) and the matching
                 buildscript.repositories AppLovin maven URL — gradle
                 plugin classpath is not an artifact dependency.

                 Consumer app minSdk 23.
    -->
    <iosPods>
        <iosPod name="DaroObjCBridge" version="2.0.0-rc.5" />
    </iosPods>
    <androidPackages>
        <androidPackage spec="so.daro:daro-sdk:2.0.0-rc.2">
            <repositories>
                <repository>https://artifacts.applovin.com/android</repository>
                <repository>https://artifact.bytedance.com/repository/pangle</repository>
                <repository>https://verve.jfrog.io/artifactory/verve-gradle-release</repository>
                <repository>https://android-sdk.is.com</repository>
                <repository>https://dl-maven-android.mintegral.com/repository/mbridge_android_sdk_oversea</repository>
                <repository>https://repo.premiumads.net/artifactory/mobile-ads-sdk/</repository>
                <repository>https://repo.pubmatic.com/artifactory/public-repos</repository>
                <repository>https://maven.ogury.co</repository>
            </repositories>
        </androidPackage>
    </androidPackages>
</dependencies>
